      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Monitor the incision site for excessive swelling, discharge, or signs of infection, and closely watch for decreased appetite, lethargy, or signs of colic internally. Withholding hay and grain for the first 12–24 hours followed by gradual reintroduction of small amounts of hay and water is the standard recovery protocol. If you notice worsening symptoms or a high temperature, contact your veterinarian immediately.",
